@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Driver Companion App"; var refs = ViewBag.DemoReferences as IReadOnlyList<string> ?? Array.Empty<string>(); var apkExists = ViewBag.ApkExists as bool? ?? false; }
<div class="sp-toolbar"><div><span class="sp-badge sp-badge--ai">Primary driver channel · Android APK/web/mobile API</span><h1>Smart Port Driver Companion App</h1><p>The Driver Companion APK, web companion, and token-secured mobile API are the reliable driver communication loop. WhatsApp Cloud API remains connector-ready for sandbox/live-test messaging, but it is not required for judging.</p></div><div class="sp-toolbar__actions"><a href="/driver/demo" class="sp-btn sp-btn--primary">Open web driver companion</a><a href="/fleet/notifications" class="sp-btn sp-btn--outline">Notification history</a></div></div>
<div class="sp-grid sp-grid--4"><article class="sp-card"><h2>1. Android APK</h2><p>Native Kotlin source at <code>mobile/SmartPortDriverCompanion</code> logs in through <code>/api/mobile/auth/demo-login</code> and calls backend mobile APIs.</p></article><article class="sp-card"><h2>2. Web companion</h2><p>Use <a href="/driver/demo">/driver/demo</a> for status, confirmations, Copilot prompts and location check-ins without APK installation.</p></article><article class="sp-card"><h2>3. Mobile API proof</h2><p>Token header <code>X-SmartPort-Mobile-Token</code> protects truck status, notifications, confirmations, Copilot and location check-ins.</p></article><article class="sp-card"><h2>4. Optional WhatsApp</h2><p>Connector-ready sandbox/live-test integration only. Production requires WhatsApp Business setup, opt-in/templates, and billing.</p></article></div>
<div class="sp-grid sp-grid--2"><article class="sp-card sp-premium-panel"><h2>Companion capabilities</h2><ul class="sp-checklist"><li>Backend setup/login with editable URL</li><li>Demo code quick-fill: <code>culltron-driver-2026</code></li><li>Demo reference quick-fill: <code>SPQ-2026-0042</code></li><li>Shows truck registration, driver, fleet operator, booking/reference, instruction, gate, staging zone, queue number, status, ETA, delay risk, idling and CO₂ impact</li><li>Posts Ready, Arrived at Staging, Delayed 20, Report Issue, Confirm Instruction and Location Check-in actions</li><li>Fetches notification history and backend Driver Copilot responses</li><li>Stores no Gemini API key, WhatsApp token, phone number or provider credential on device</li></ul></article><article class="sp-card"><h2>Backend URL instructions</h2><dl class="driver-dl"><dt>Android emulator local Docker</dt><dd><code>http://10.0.2.2:8080</code></dd><dt>Codespaces / DigitalOcean / live</dt><dd>Paste the deployed HTTPS app URL into the APK login screen.</dd><dt>Driver code/reference</dt><dd><code>culltron-driver-2026</code> · <code>SPQ-2026-0042</code></dd></dl></article></div>
<article class="sp-card sp-download-panel"><div><span class="sp-badge sp-badge--green">@(apkExists ? "APK ready" : "APK workflow ready")</span><h2>APK availability</h2>@if(apkExists){<p>Debug APK is available for demo installation.</p><a class="sp-btn sp-btn--primary" href="/downloads/SmartPortDriverCompanion.apk">Download SmartPortDriverCompanion.apk</a>}else{<p class="sp-alert sp-alert--info">Android companion source and APK workflow are ready. Core driver demo works through web companion and mobile API.</p><p class="sp-muted">CI uploads the debug APK artifact from <code>.github/workflows/build-android-apk.yml</code>. If a local Android SDK is available, run <code>cd mobile/SmartPortDriverCompanion && ./gradlew assembleDebug</code> or <code>gradle assembleDebug</code>, then copy the APK to <code>src/SmartPort.Web/wwwroot/downloads/SmartPortDriverCompanion.apk</code>.</p>}</div></article>
<div class="sp-grid sp-grid--2"><article class="sp-card"><h2>Mobile API proof path</h2><ol class="sp-steps"><li><code>POST /api/mobile/auth/demo-login</code></li><li><code>GET /api/mobile/truck/status/SPQ-2026-0042</code></li><li><code>GET /api/mobile/notifications/SPQ-2026-0042</code></li><li><code>POST /api/mobile/driver/confirm-status</code></li><li><code>POST /api/mobile/driver/location-checkin</code></li><li><code>POST /api/mobile/copilot/driver</code></li></ol></article><article class="sp-card"><h2>Demo references</h2><p>Use one of these references in the web companion, Android app or mobile API smoke tests:</p><div class="ack-grid">@foreach(var r in refs){<code class="sp-chip">@r</code>}</div><p><a class="sp-btn sp-btn--outline" href="/health/integrations">Open integration health</a></p></article></div>
